rules:
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that all architectural decisions are expressed via a structured
    YAML schema rather than narrative text to ensure machine-readability and consistency.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Establishes Architecture Decision Records (ADR) as the primary authority
    for decisions; all other artifacts must be derived from them to prevent metadata
    drift.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Enforces that all new patterns are initially classified as 'supporting'
    by default to ensure validation before potential promotion to core.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Prohibits the consolidation of patterns from different architectural layers
    to maintain clear separation of concerns (e.g., governance vs. execution).
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the priority for rule resolution where Global Rules take precedence
    over Project Rules, and Project Rules take precedence over Prompt Rules.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires that any pattern derived from heuristics includes at least one
    linked signal as evidence to ensure grounding in observed behavior.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Synchronizes pattern maturity levels with governance decision statuses
    to prevent premature promotion and ensure consistent state interpretation.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: "Defines mandatory criteria\u2014recurrence, system impact, reusability,\
    \ and stability\u2014and evidence requirements for promoting a signal to a pattern."
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Specifies that generated documents like AEM and AID are summaries and must
    not hold authoritative state, which resides in durable source artifacts.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that workflows comply with the CAS Execution Model, ensuring separation
    between orchestration (Runner) and reasoning (Workflow).
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Derives the lifecycle stage of any architectural item directly from its
    decision status; items only map to 'DONE' when 'accepted'.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires projects to participate in the shared Knowledge Workspace and
    prohibits the duplication of global governance structures.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Establishes Architecture Work as the authoritative source for planning
    state; generated artifacts must derive status from this registry.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures the Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) reflects and never contradicts
    decisions recorded in Architecture Decision Records (ADR).
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Enforces human-in-the-loop governance by requiring that all system-proposed
    architectural decisions be explicitly approved by an architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires that all architectural decisions are persisted as structured ADRs
    before they are reflected in any other system artifacts.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Limits 'core' pattern status to foundational architectural primitives,
    excluding specific strategies or implementation-level approaches.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that pattern promotion to core must be supported by strong evidence
    from multiple sources or systems.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the semantic contract for standardizing language around intent,
    decisions, and system state to ensure clarity and traceability.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
